<div id="2026-11-06-consignment-replacement" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-06 — A count now opens the replacement consignment, and says so</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Applying a location count used to bill the partner and stop. It now also opens a replacement consignment (<code>REPL-&lt;site&gt;-&lt;count&gt;</code>, status <em>open</em>) with one line per item, <em>qty sent</em> = units sold, stamps <code>inventory_location_counts.consignment_id</code>, points the queued top-up print jobs at that consignment, and creates a todo in the Monachee Coop project ("Replace sold stock - consignment #N") so the refill appears in the work list instead of waiting to be found on a traveler.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Consignment 8 (April) and every count before this one left <code>consignment_id</code> and <code>traveller_id</code> NULL, even though both columns existed. Nothing to pull, nothing to print, nothing to put on a sheet. Count #3 applied on 2026-11-05 produced INV-3D-0001 and no replacement.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>How verified.</strong> End-to-end run inside a transaction that was rolled back: a two-colour test count reported sold 1, created consignment <code>REPL-3D-8</code>, line item 41 <em>qty_sent 1.00</em>, invoice INV-3D-0002 total 1.78, print job #194 linked to that consignment, and todo "Replace sold stock - consignment #12". After rollback the consignment, job and todo counts were unchanged.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Also.</strong> <code>printing_3d_jobs</code> costing widened so components are stored unrounded: <code>filament_cost</code>, <code>printer_cost</code>, <code>electricity_cost</code> declare <code>decimal(10,4)</code>; <code>total_cost</code> stays <code>decimal(10,2)</code> so rounding happens once, at the end. Columns need an Update Table on <code>/admin/schema_compare</code> to pick this up.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/ConsignmentCountApply.pm</code> (replacement block, <code>_notify_replacement</code>), <code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/Printing3dJob.pm</code> (decimal widths), <code>root/Documentation/Inventory/consignment.tt</code> §8 Replacement After a Sale.</p>
</div>
